## 2. Tech Stack (with reasoning, not just buzzwords)

### 2.1 Frontend — Patient App
| Layer | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Framework | **React + PWA (installable, offline-cache via Service Workers)** | Rural users won't download a heavy native app; a PWA installs from a link/QR, works on cheap Android, degrades gracefully on 2G/3G |
| State/offline | IndexedDB + Workbox | Lets referral status, appointment info, instructions be viewed with zero connectivity |
| UI | Large-tap targets, icon+text nav, Devnagari/regional fonts | Matches your mockup — low-literacy-friendly |
| Voice | On-device STT trigger → cloud fallback (Bhashini API) | "Need help? 🎤 Speak" bubble in your dashboard needs low-latency local option first |

### 2.2 Frontend — ASHA/ANM/PHC Worker App
| Layer | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Framework | **React Native or Flutter (real offline-first app, not just PWA)** | Field workers need camera (photo of prescription/report), GPS, and true background sync — PWA alone is weaker here |
| Local DB | **SQLite / WatermelonDB** with a sync engine (e.g. CouchDB/PouchDB-style replication or custom delta-sync) | This is the single most important technical decision in the whole product — see §4 |
| Auth | OTP + optional biometric, works fully offline once logged in once | Matches your onboarding screens |

### 2.3 Receiving Facility Panel + Admin Dashboard
- **React (web only, facilities have desks/desktops)** — no offline requirement here, these sit at hospitals with power/internet.
- Charting: Recharts/Chart.js for the metrics in your admin dashboard (referral completion rate, bottlenecks, follow-up rates).

### 2.4 Backend
| Layer | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|
| API | **Node.js (NestJS) or Python (FastAPI)** | Either is fine; FastAPI is a slight edge if your AI layer is Python-native (easier to co-locate ML calls) |
| Core logic | **Referral State Machine as an explicit service**, not buried in CRUD | This IS your product. Model it as a first-class finite-state machine: `Created → Accepted → Scheduled → Reached → Consulted → Treated → FollowUpDue → FollowUpCompleted`, each transition timestamped, actor-logged, and reversible/auditable |
| Auth | OTP-based (Twilio/MSG91 or India-specific SMS gateway) + JWT | Matches your OTP screens; no passwords — rural users won't manage them |
| Queue/jobs | Redis + BullMQ (or Celery if Python) | Needed for: overdue-follow-up checks, reminder scheduling, sync reconciliation jobs |
| Realtime | WebSockets or Firebase Cloud Messaging for push | Facility panel needs to see incoming referrals live |

### 2.5 Database
- **PostgreSQL** — relational, because referrals/patients/facilities/appointments are inherently relational and you need strong consistency for a *closure* engine (you cannot have ambiguous referral states).
- **Redis** — caching + job queues + OTP short-lived storage.
- **Object storage (S3-compatible)** — for scanned reports, prescription photos.
- **Audit/event log table** (append-only) — every state transition, every AI suggestion accepted/rejected. This is what makes the product defensible to a health department (traceability), and it's cheap to build if you design for it from day one.

### 2.6 Infra / DevOps
- Containerized (Docker) → deploy on **any cloud (AWS/GCP/Azure) or state data-center-friendly infra** — health data sovereignty matters for government pilots, so keep the option to self-host on Indian infra (NIC cloud / MeghRaj) open in your architecture doc even if you build on AWS for the hackathon.
- CI/CD: GitHub Actions.
- Monitoring: basic (Sentry for errors, simple uptime checks) — don't over-engineer this for a hackathon demo.

### 2.7 Integrations (this is what makes it "real" to a jury)
| Integration | Purpose | Hackathon reality |
|---|---|---|
| **ABDM (ABHA, HFR, HPR sandbox)** | Patient ID, facility registry, provider registry | ABDM has a public **sandbox** — integrate against that, don't fake it. This alone differentiates you from 90% of SIH teams who only claim ABDM compliance in slides |
| **eSanjeevani** | If a referral resolves into a teleconsult, hand off instead of duplicating | No public API for teams typically — simulate this handoff with a mocked adapter, be honest about it in your pitch |
| **Bhashini** | Voice + translation for Indian languages | Public API, genuinely usable in a hackathon |
| **SMS/WhatsApp Business API** | Reminders reach patients even without app opened | Critical — many patients won't open the app for a follow-up reminder, but they'll read an SMS |

